# W22-U2 (Opus defense unit U2, codex #6 belt-and-braces): pin LF for every path the publish pipeline
# treats as a byte-exact input. The ACTUAL fix for codex #6 (a fresh Windows checkout with
# core.autocrlf=true corrupting find/replace and overlay content) is scripts/publish-public.cjs reading
# every publish input from the frozen Git OID via `git show`/`git cat-file` -- which is immune to the
# checkout's own core.autocrlf setting entirely, since that only affects files materialized onto disk,
# never a blob read straight out of the object database. This file is added only as a second,
# independent line of defense (per the defense doc's explicit instruction NOT to rely on .gitattributes
# alone) and to keep a plain `git diff`/`git show` of these paths stable across contributors' local
# autocrlf settings. Added only after confirming it does not reformat/touch any existing tracked blob
# (`git add --renormalize` produced zero changes) -- see this unit's own build report.
publish-overrides/** text eol=lf
publish.manifest.json text eol=lf
scripts/** text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
